    "problem_statement": "TextFSMOptions value gets incremented by 1 causing TypeError\n\nWhen creating TextFSMOptions instances, the value parameter is being incremented by 1 in the constructor, which causes issues when the value is expected to be used as-is for bitwise operations or other numeric comparisons.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport textfsm\n\n# Create a TextFSMValue with options\nv = textfsm.TextFSMValue(options_class=textfsm.TextFSMOptions)\nv.Parse('Value Required beer (\\\\S+)')\n\n# This should work but fails due to the +1 increment\nprint(v.OptionNames())\n```\n\nThe issue manifests when parsing FSM templates that use options like `Required`, `Filldown`, etc. The options parsing fails with `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s)` because the numeric values used for bitwise operations are off by 1.\n\nThis affects any template parsing that involves options, making it impossible to use features like:\n- `Value Required fieldname (regex)`  \n- `Value Filldown fieldname (regex)`\n- `Value Required,Filldown fieldname (regex)`\n\nThe error occurs during option processing where the incremented values cause type mismatches in bitwise operations used to determine which options are set."
